.TH XIL\-PARSED\-CSV "1" "2026\-07\-02" "xil\-pipeline 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
xil\-parsed\-csv \- export parsed_<TAG>.json entries to CSV, one row per entry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xil\-parsed\-csv
[\-h] [\fI\,PATH\/\fR] [\-\-output FILE] [\-\-json]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a
.B parsed_<TAG>.json
file produced by
.B xil\-parse
and writes a flat CSV (or JSON array) with one row per script entry.  Columns
include sequence number, section, type, speaker, text, direction type, and
SFX source path.
.PP
When
.I PATH
is omitted, scans
.B parsed/\fR\fI<slug>\fR/
under the current workspace root for the most recent parsed JSON matching the
active show.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PATH
Path to a parsed_*.json file or parsed directory (default: workspace parsed/<slug>/)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR, \fB\-o\fR \fI\,FILE\/\fR
Write CSV output to FILE (default: stdout)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output a JSON array to stdout \(em no banner, safe to pipe to jq
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Export the active episode's parsed JSON to CSV:
.B xil parsed\-csv
.TP
Export a specific parsed JSON:
.B xil parsed\-csv parsed/the413/parsed_the413_S01E01.json \-\-output script.csv
.TP
Pipe to jq to list all direction lines:
.B xil parsed\-csv \-\-json | jq '.[] | select(.type == "direction")'
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xil (1),
.BR xil\-parse (1),
.BR xil\-csv\-join (1),
.BR xil\-sfx\-csv (1)
.SH AUTHOR
John Brissette <xilcmd@gmail.com>
